<title>DENMARK: Danish May North Sea gas production rises 3.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish May North Sea gas production rises 3.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) production of gas from its North Sea fields rose 3.7 percent in May 1997 to 509 million cubic metres from 491 million cubic metres in April, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>   (Million cubic metres)   May 97    April 97     May 96</p>
<p>    Total production	     509	  491	  460</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the fourth-biggest offshore gas producer in western Europe after Norway, Britain and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively.</p>
<p>-- Steve Weizman, Copenhagen Newsroom 45-33-969650</p>
</text>
